"program_narrative": "ERRHANDL is a batch template program (src/templates/error/error-handling.cbl) that demonstrates a standard error-handling pattern. It uses no files and no copybooks; all data is in WORKING-STORAGE (return-code constants, an error message buffer, error flags, error counters and three message texts). After resetting its flags and counters it runs, unconditionally and in order, a warning, an error, a severe-error and an abend scenario; each one counts the event, sets a severity, number and message text and logs them to the console through 8100-LOG-ERROR. The abend scenario finishes by calling the Language Environment service CEE3ABD with RC-CRITICAL, which requests abnormal termination. If control comes back, 8000-CHECK-FINAL-STATUS sets the program return code to 12, 8, 4 or 0 according to the highest error level counted (severe, error, warning, none). Error conditions handled: warning, error, severe error and unrecoverable error (abend).",
